-- title:
--   Kernel ideal sheaf of a closed immersion into Pⁿ_A
-- statement:
--   Let $n$ be a natural number, $A$ a commutative ring, and write $\mathbb{P}^n_A$ for `Proj` of the graded ring of homogeneous components of $A[x_0,\dots,x_n] =$ `MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) A`. Let $Z$ be a scheme, $\iota : Z \to \mathbb{P}^n_A$ a morphism which is a closed immersion, $m$ a natural number, and $\mathcal{I}$ an ideal sheaf datum on $\mathbb{P}^n_A$ (a `Scheme.IdealSheafData`, i.e. a compatible family of ideals on the affine opens). Write $J$ for the ideal of $A[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ generated by those polynomials $F$ which are homogeneous of some degree $d \ge m$ and satisfy, for every $i$, that the section $F/x_i^{d}$ of the standard chart $D_+(x_i)$ — the image under `Proj.awayToSection` of the homogeneous localisation with numerator $F$ and denominator $x_i^{d}$ — pulls back to $0$ under $\iota^{\sharp}$ on $D_+(x_i)$. The hypothesis on $\mathcal{I}$ is that for every $i \in \{0,\dots,n\}$ its ideal on the affine open $D_+(x_i)$ is generated by the sections $F/x_i^{d}$ with $F \in J$ homogeneous of degree $d$. The conclusion is that $\mathcal{I}$ coincides with $\iota$`.ker`, the kernel ideal sheaf of $\iota$.
--
--   This identifies the ideal sheaf of a closed subscheme of projective space with the one cut out, chart by chart, by the degree-$\ge m$ part of its homogeneous ideal, for an arbitrary truncation bound $m$; it is the scheme-theoretic form of the correspondence between closed subschemes of $\operatorname{Proj}$ and saturated homogeneous ideals. It is used in the construction of closed subschemes of $\mathbb{P}^n_A$ with prescribed behaviour for the Hilbert functor, in particular by the statements producing a finitely generated homogeneous ideal whose chart ideals compute $\iota$`.ker` and by the flatness and Hilbert-function statements for the Hilbert functor.
